{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וירא והנה באר בשדה", :translit "va-yar ve-hineh be'er ba-sadeh", :gloss "and he looked and behold a well in the field"} {:he "כמו שאנכי יפת תואר", :translit "ka-mo she-anokhi yefat to'ar", :gloss "just as I am beautiful of form"} {:he "ונזדמנתי על הבאר", :translit "ve-nizdamneti al ha-be'er", :gloss "and I chanced upon the well"} {:he "כן יהיה לך מבנות אחי", :translit "ken yihyeh lakh mi-benot ahi", :gloss "so shall it be for you from my brother's daughters"}], :mechanities [{:kind "other", :note "Rivkah instructs Yaakov that the sign of his destined match at the well mirrors her own experience"}], :frame {:text "Rivkah encounters Eliezer at a well and is identified as beautiful of form (Genesis 24:16). She now tells Yaakov that just as her own match happened at a well, so too his destined match among Lavan's daughters will be recognized at the well by the same sign.", :sources ["Genesis 24:16" "Genesis 24:15-20"]}, :mechanisms []} {:quotes [{:he "והנה באר בשדה", :translit "ve-hineh be'er ba-sadeh", :gloss "and behold a well in the field"} {:he "הבאר שהיה לישראל במדבר", :translit "ha-be'er she-hayah le-yisra'el ba-midbar", :gloss "the well that Israel had in the wilderness"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Allusion: the well of Genesis 29:2 foreshadows the well of Israel in the wilderness"}], :frame {:text "Israel's well in the wilderness is associated with Miriam; the verse states Israel arrived at the well (Numbers 21:16-18) and the Talmud identifies this well as one given on Miriam's merit (Taanit 9a).", :sources ["Numbers 21:16-18" "Taanit 9a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "שלשה עדרי", :translit "shloshah adrei", :gloss "three flocks"} {:he "אהרן ומשה ומרים", :translit "aharon u-moshe u-miryam", :gloss "Aaron and Moses and Miriam"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "שלשה עדרי", :b "אהרן ומשה ומרים"}], :frame {:text "The three leaders Aaron, Moses, and Miriam each correspond to one of three divine gifts Israel received in the wilderness: the pillar of cloud, the manna, and the well (Taanit 9a). Ba'al HaTurim connects the three flocks to these same three figures.", :sources ["Taanit 9a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "כי מן הבאר ההוא", :translit "ki min ha-be'er ha-hu", :gloss "for from that well"} {:he "משה", :translit "moshe", :gloss "Moses"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "כי מן הבאר ההוא", :b "משה"}], :frame nil} {:quotes [{:he "והאבן", :translit "ve-ha-even", :gloss "and the stone"} {:he "ב' בפרשה", :translit "bet ba-parashah", :gloss "two times in the parashah"} {:he "שני לוחות אבנים", :translit "shnei luchot avanim", :gloss "two stone tablets"} {:he "ז' פעמים באר בפרשה", :translit "zet pa'amim be'er ba-parashah", :gloss "seven times well in the parashah"} {:he "ז' ימי החג", :translit "zet yemei ha-chag", :gloss "seven days of the Festival"} {:he "שבעה שקורין בתורה בשבת", :translit "shiv'ah she-korin ba-torah ba-shabbat", :gloss "seven who read from the Torah on Sabbath"} {:he "ה' מהם פי הבאר", :translit "hei mehem pi ha-be'er", :gloss "five of them mouth of the well"} {:he "ה' שקורין ביום טוב", :translit "hei she-korin be-yom tov", :gloss "five who read on a Festival"} {:he "ג' מהם מעל פי הבאר", :translit "gimel mehem me'al pi ha-be'er", :gloss "three of them above the mouth of the well"} {:he "ג' שקורין בחול", :translit "gimel she-korin ba-chol", :gloss "three who read on a weekday"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["והאבן"]} {:kind :masorah, :count 7, :occurrences ["באר"]} {:kind :other, :note "Seven occurrences of 'well' correspond to seven days of Sukkot (water libation) and seven Torah readers on Sabbath; five with 'mouth of the well' correspond to five readers on Festival; three with 'above the mouth of the well' correspond to three readers on weekday"}], :frame {:text "Mishnah Sukkah 4:9 describes water libation rites on Sukkot. Mishnah Megillah 3:2 and Talmud Bavli Megillah 23a specify that seven read from the Torah on Sabbath, five on a Festival,